From c990ca971a31690ee5ddec1ee68b2571aa20b998 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: moto <j3tm0t0@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:50:27 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] bootwait: real stage progress instead of the decorative track
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The [Pico W] ━◆━ [X68000 Z] row is replaced by "Wi-Fi ━━ SMB ━━ HDS ━━
起動" (8 ━ per segment, centred):
- current stage from sysstatus (0-1 Wi-Fi, 2-3 SMB, 4-5 HDS);
  completed labels/segments light blue, the current label white,
  stages not reached muted blue (palette 1 slightly lighter);
- in the current segment the ◆ moves every poll; while SMB waits for
  the next retry the segment fills toward it from the Pico's
  ms-until-retry over the 5 s retry period, ◆ at the fill head;
- on BW_READY all stages (incl. 起動) light up and stay for 0.5 s before
  the screen is restored and the real IPL runs.
The ring pulse stays (now in draw_stages).
waiter_test.py: labels, centring, the exact SMB fill for 3.2 s left,
colours of done/current/next, the moving ◆, all lit for >= 0.5 s before
the hand-over.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PrGdt1XK1exBgERrMmLA1u
